The Security Council,
Recalling all its previous relevant resolutions and statements of its President concerning Lebanon, including resolutions 425 (1978), 426 (1978), 1701 (2006) and 2749 (2024),
Reaffirming its strong commitment to the sovereignty, territorial integrity, political independence and unity of Lebanon within its internationally recognized borders,
Reaffirming its support for the full implementation of resolution 1701 (2006) and the relevant provisions of the Taif Accords, and stressing that the framework of resolution 1701 (2006) remains the basis for a permanent ceasefire and a long-term solution,
Recalling the ceasefire agreement of 27 November 2024 and the need for its full implementation, including the withdrawal of Israeli forces from Lebanese territory and the deployment of the Lebanese Armed Forces throughout southern Lebanon and to the Blue Line,
Welcoming the decision of the Government of Lebanon of 7 August 2025 to approve a plan to assert the authority of the Lebanese State and the monopoly on the use of force over all Lebanese territory, including the disarmament of all armed groups by the end of 2025, and encouraging its swift and faithful implementation,
Deeply concerned by continuing tensions and by violations of the cessation of hostilities and of resolution 1701 (2006), including continued Israeli airstrikes and incursions in Lebanese territory, attacks from Lebanese territory against Israel, and the presence of unauthorized weapons outside the control of the Lebanese State,
Condemning all attacks against United Nations personnel and demanding accountability, and recalling the need for all parties to protect civilians, humanitarian personnel and medical personnel, and to ensure safe and unimpeded humanitarian access,
Stressing the critical role of the United Nations Interim Force in Lebanon (UNIFIL), in cooperation with the Lebanese Armed Forces, in supporting the implementation of resolution 1701 (2006), including through monitoring, reporting and verification, and underlining the need for UNIFIL to have freedom of movement and unrestricted access,
Emphasizing the importance of the safe, voluntary and dignified return of displaced persons in accordance with international law, and the need to address the humanitarian needs of the Lebanese people,
Determining that the situation in Lebanon continues to constitute a threat to international peace and security,
Acting under Chapter VII of the Charter of the United Nations,
1. Decides to extend the present mandate of the United Nations Interim Force in Lebanon (UNIFIL) until 31 August 2026, and decides that UNIFIL shall continue to implement its mandate in accordance with resolutions 425 (1978), 426 (1978) and 1701 (2006) and this resolution;
2. Reaffirms its commitment to the full implementation of resolution 1701 (2006) and the relevant provisions of the Taif Accords, calls for a full cessation of hostilities and a permanent ceasefire, and calls upon all parties to respect the Blue Line and to refrain from any violations and from acts of escalation;
3. Calls for the full and timely implementation of the ceasefire agreement of 27 November 2024 and subsequent arrangements, including the full withdrawal of Israeli forces from Lebanese territory and the deployment of the Lebanese Armed Forces throughout southern Lebanon and to the Blue Line, in close coordination with UNIFIL;
4. Welcomes the decision of the Government of Lebanon of 7 August 2025 to approve a plan to assert the authority and monopoly on the use of force of the Lebanese State over all Lebanese territory, including the disarmament of all armed groups by the end of 2025, calls for its swift and faithful implementation, and calls upon all parties in Lebanon to support the Lebanese Armed Forces and refrain from acts that undermine State authority;
5. Calls upon Member States to provide timely and coordinated support to the Lebanese Armed Forces and the Government of Lebanon, including through training, equipment and technical assistance, to enable the Lebanese Armed Forces to assume its responsibilities under resolution 1701 (2006) and the ceasefire agreement;
6. Demands that all parties comply fully with their obligations under international humanitarian law and international human rights law, protect civilians, and refrain from attacks against civilians, humanitarian personnel, medical personnel and United Nations personnel; and demands that all parties ensure the safety, security and freedom of movement of UNIFIL personnel, and cease immediately any attacks or threats against peacekeepers;
7. Condemns all violations of the cessation of hostilities and of resolution 1701 (2006), calls for accountability for all such violations, and urges all parties to cooperate fully with UNIFIL and the United Nations to investigate and report on violations, including attacks against UNIFIL and Lebanese Armed Forces personnel;
8. Requests the Secretary-General to continue to report every four months on the implementation of resolution 1701 (2006) and this resolution, including on violations, UNIFIL’s ability to implement its mandate, the deployment and capabilities of the Lebanese Armed Forces, progress in the implementation of the decision of the Government of Lebanon of 7 August 2025, and the humanitarian situation;
9. Requests the Secretary-General to take all necessary measures to ensure the safety and security of UNIFIL personnel and to continue to strengthen security arrangements for UNIFIL positions and patrols, in consultation with troop-contributing countries;
10. Decides to remain actively seized of the matter.

