Determining that the situation in Lebanon continues to constitute a threat to international peace and security,
Acting under Chapter VII of the Charter of the United Nations,
1. Decides to extend the present mandate of the United Nations Interim Force in Lebanon (UNIFIL) until 31 August 2026, and decides that UNIFIL shall continue to implement its mandate in accordance with resolutions 425 (1978), 426 (1978) and 1701 (2006) and this resolution;
2. Reaffirms its commitment to the full implementation of resolution 1701 (2006) and the relevant provisions of the Taif Accords, calls for a full cessation of hostilities and a permanent ceasefire, and calls upon all parties to respect the Blue Line and to refrain from any violations, including violations of Lebanese airspace, and from acts of escalation;
3. Calls for the full and timely implementation of the ceasefire agreement of 27 November 2024 and subsequent arrangements, including the immediate, full and complete withdrawal of Israeli forces from all Lebanese territory, and the full deployment of the Lebanese Armed Forces throughout southern Lebanon and to the Blue Line, in close coordination with UNIFIL, and calls for a defined timeline for the implementation of these steps;
4. Demands the full and swift implementation of the decision of the Government of Lebanon of 7 August 2025 to assert the authority and monopoly on the use of force of the Lebanese State over all Lebanese territory by the end of 2025, in full respect of Lebanon's sovereignty, territorial integrity and political independence, in accordance with Lebanese law and the Constitution and through a Lebanese-led political process based on national consensus and free from external interference, including through the disarmament and dismantlement of all armed groups, including Hezbollah; calls upon all parties in Lebanon to support the Lebanese Armed Forces and refrain from acts that undermine State authority; and demands that Hezbollah immediately cease all armed activity and cooperate with the Lebanese Armed Forces;
5. Condemns in the strongest terms Hezbollah's continued attacks against Israel and violations of resolution 1701 (2006) and the 27 November 2024 ceasefire, demands that Hezbollah cease all attacks and withdraw all its forces and weapons north of the Litani River, and calls upon all Member States to support the Lebanese Armed Forces, at the request of the Government of Lebanon, in dismantling unauthorized military infrastructure and preventing the resupply of arms;
6. Calls upon all States, in particular Iran, to cease the supply, sale or transfer of arms and related materiel to Hezbollah and other armed groups in Lebanon, and to respect Lebanon's sovereignty and territorial integrity;
7. Calls upon Member States to provide timely and coordinated support to the Lebanese Armed Forces and the Government of Lebanon, including through training, equipment and technical assistance, at the request of and with the consent of the Government of Lebanon, in close coordination with the Lebanese Armed Forces, and in full respect for Lebanon's sovereignty and territorial integrity, to enable the Lebanese Armed Forces to assume its responsibilities under resolution 1701 (2006) and the ceasefire agreement;
8. Demands that all parties comply fully with their obligations under international humanitarian law and international human rights law, protect civilians, and refrain from attacks against civilians, humanitarian personnel, medical personnel and United Nations personnel, and ensure safe, unimpeded and sustained humanitarian access to all civilians in need; demands that all parties ensure the safety, security and freedom of movement of UNIFIL personnel, and unhindered and unrestricted access throughout its area of operations, including to the Blue Line, and reaffirms the inviolability of United Nations premises and installations;
9. Condemns all violations of the cessation of hostilities and of resolution 1701 (2006), including attacks from Lebanese territory against Israel, in particular by Hezbollah, and continuing Israeli airstrikes, incursions and violations of Lebanese airspace and territorial waters; calls for the immediate cessation of all such violations and for accountability; recalls that attacks against United Nations peacekeepers may constitute war crimes and calls for their prompt, independent and impartial investigation; and urges all parties to cooperate fully with UNIFIL and the United Nations to investigate and report on violations, including attacks against UNIFIL and Lebanese Armed Forces personnel;
10. Calls upon all parties to ensure the safe, voluntary and dignified return of displaced persons in accordance with international law and to facilitate unhindered humanitarian access to affected populations;
11. Requests the Secretary-General to continue to report every four months on the implementation of resolution 1701 (2006) and this resolution, including on violations, arms smuggling and the supply of weapons to armed groups, the safety and security of UNIFIL personnel, impediments to UNIFIL's freedom of movement and access, including any obstruction by Hezbollah or other armed groups, UNIFIL's ability to implement its mandate, the deployment and capabilities of the Lebanese Armed Forces, progress in the implementation of the decision of the Government of Lebanon of 7 August 2025, and the humanitarian situation, including obstacles to humanitarian access and to the safe, voluntary and dignified return of displaced persons, and the impact on children and other vulnerable groups;
12. Requests the Secretary-General to take all necessary measures to ensure the safety and security of UNIFIL personnel and to continue to strengthen security arrangements for UNIFIL positions and patrols, in close and timely consultation with troop-contributing countries, including on security arrangements and any adjustments to UNIFIL's configuration, and to keep troop-contributing countries fully informed of security measures affecting their personnel;
13. Decides to remain actively seized of the matter.

